   "body": "/claim cloud/m4q-reliab-opus\n\nRe-checked on `dev-swift` @ 1b6f98f0: the problem still holds. `DraftContext`, `TopicID` and `CategoryID` use synthesized coding. `DraftStore.loadedState` sets the whole file aside on any `DecodingError`. No literal file pins the format. No open PR touches `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRStorage/Drafts/` or its tests.\n\nPlan:\n- A golden test of the v1 file, captured from the current code with one draft per `DraftContext` case. It checks that this file reads back to the expected drafts, and that the writer still produces the same JSON (compared as parsed JSON, not bytes).\n- `DraftDocument` decodes its drafts entry by entry. An entry it cannot read (an unknown context, a bad date) no longer sets the file aside. It is also not dropped: it is kept as raw JSON and written back on the next save, so a draft from a newer build is not lost. Test: `anUnknownContextDropsOneDraftNotTheFile`, which is red today.\n- `page` stays in `reply` (part of the key and of the v1 file). A comment will say the app always writes 1 and that the key is on disk.\n- Draft PR with a Fable review.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
